Description: Selviana Desktop Environment - SDE Core
 SDE (Selviana Desktop Environment) is a lightweight desktop environment
 developed by the Selviana DE Project, with a Rust configuration core and
 autostart helper, a C++17 interface using SDE-FLTK, cairo and Xlib, and a
 source-built SDE WM (Openbox) and SDE compositor (picom). It is built and
 tested on Debian testing.
 .
 SDE Core is the desktop itself, without the applications:
  * sde-session and startsde: the session, with crash recovery, a rescue
    dialog, XDG autostart and a system check (sde-session --check);
  * sde-panel: taskbar, Start menu, search, quick settings, calendar and
    tray; sde-desktop: wallpaper and desktop icons;
  * sde-settings (sde-control-center): the Control Center, with Users &
    Avatar, appearance, displays, sound, power, network, keyboard and
    mouse; sde-display-settings: monitor profiles, resolution and scale;
  * sde-notifyd (notifications), sde-run (Alt+F2) and sde-logout (log out,
    lock, suspend, restart and shut down);
  * sde-power (battery, lid, idle and brightness) and sde-lock (the screen
    locker, PAM service sde-lock);
  * sde-core: the SDE core controller (org.selviana.Core) that connects
    the session, the panel, the Control Center and the applications;
  * sde-watchdog and sde-force-close: Wait or Force Close for programs
    that stop responding;
  * sde-touchscreen: keeps a touch screen on its own display and shows
    touches (SDE-FLTK takes the gestures in every program);
  * Software Updater (sde-update), Welcome, Driver Manager, System Reports,
    SDE System Monitor, Debrun (.deb files) and sde-appimage;
  * sde-xsettingsd, sde-polkit-agent, the file chooser portal and
    sde-autostart;
  * SDE WM (Openbox) and SDE compositor (picom), the SDE Graphite, Fluent
    and Glass themes, the SDE icons, wallpapers, logo and shared data.
 .
 The applications are packages of their own: liria, xanara, niny, merkadu,
 sde-calculator, taca, sde-photo and sde-gallery. The sde-desktop
 metapackage installs SDE Core, every application, GNOME Terminal and the
 login screen. Select "SDE-Desktop" in your display manager to start it.
 This is an alpha release meant for testing; expect missing features.

