Recommends: sde-core
Suggests: snapd
Description: Selviana Desktop Environment - software center
 Merkadu is the software center of the Selviana Desktop Environment (SDE).
 It finds, installs, updates and removes apps from three sources in one
 search:
  * the Debian archive, through PackageKit and the archive's AppStream
    catalog;
  * Flatpak remotes: Flathub is set up when Merkadu is installed (unless
    /etc/merkadu/merkadu.conf says otherwise);
  * the Snap Store, through snapd ("Enable Snap Support" installs it).
 .
 An app offered by more than one source is shown once, with the source of
 each version, and you choose where to install it from. Merkadu has a Home
 page with highlights and recommendations, departments with subcategories,
 app pages with screenshots, the installed apps by department, app updates,
 the history of every source and a progress view with the animated SDE logo.
 All Software lists every package of the Debian archive by section and
 status, like Synaptic: several installations and removals are marked and
 applied together after a summary. The software lists are refreshed in the
 background when Merkadu opens. The SDE Start menu uses
 "merkadu --uninstall" to uninstall an app from its launcher.
 .
 Merkadu is based on Ubuntu Software Center. Installing and removing are
 authorized with polkit; Merkadu itself never runs as root.

