Description: Selviana Desktop Environment - full desktop (metapackage)
 One installation entry point for the complete Selviana Desktop Environment:
 SDE Core, every SDE application (Liria, Xanara, Niny, Merkadu, Calculator,
 Taca, Photo and Gallery), GNOME Terminal, the display server, the login
 screen and the network, sound and removable media services.
 .
 The login screen is LightDM with Slick Greeter: SDE-Desktop is the
 default session and the users are listed, without a manual login entry
 or a guest session, in SDE Graphite with the SDE logo over the login
 background of the active desktop-base theme (DebION's with
 debion-desktop-base). Login Window (lightdm-settings) changes it. A Debian
 live system starts the live user's SDE-Desktop session directly. GNOME
 Terminal is the default terminal unless the administrator chose another
 x-terminal-emulator.
 .
 SDE does not require a particular distribution. On DebION GNU/Linux the
 recommended debion-desktop-base package adds the distribution's artwork and
 network defaults; it is a separate project's package.
 .
 This metapackage installs individual maintained components rather than
 another complete desktop environment. Existing user preferences and
 distribution package sources are preserved.

