Description: Selviana Desktop Environment - transitional package
 SDE 0.2.0 Alpha 4 split the sde package into SDE Core (sde-core) and one
 package per application (liria, xanara, niny, sde-calculator, taca,
 sde-photo and sde-gallery). This transitional package installs them on
 upgrades from older versions and can be removed afterwards. The complete
 desktop is the sde-desktop package.

Package: debion-desktop-base
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         desktop-base
Recommends: network-manager,
            iproute2,
            curl,
            ca-certificates,
            systemd-timesyncd | time-daemon
Description: DebION GNU/Linux integration for SDE
 DebION GNU/Linux is a Debian-based distribution that ships the Selviana
 Desktop Environment; it is a separate project. This package holds its
 integration: its artwork and desktop defaults for desktop-base and its
 network defaults.
 .
 Makes the DebION theme the active desktop-base theme: wallpaper, lock
 screen, login screen and GRUB background follow it in every desktop
 (/usr/share/desktop-base/active-theme). It also provides the DebION vendor
 logos and emblems and a DebION Plymouth boot splash.
 .
 Debian's themes stay installed; choose another one with
 "update-alternatives --config desktop-theme".
 .
 Desktop network defaults: NetworkManager connectivity checking against
 Debian's endpoint (/usr/lib/NetworkManager/conf.d/20-debion-connectivity.conf;
 override it in /etc/NetworkManager/conf.d/), and debion-network-check, which
 explains "connected but no internet" (interfaces left to ifupdown, competing
 default routes, a broken /etc/resolv.conf, a network that needs a proxy,
 a wrong clock, broken IPv6). On first installation, interfaces that
 /etc/network/interfaces configures with plain DHCP or a wpa-ssid/wpa-psk
 Wi-Fi network move to NetworkManager at the next boot (backups in
 /var/backups/debion-network; static, bridge, bond and VLAN setups are left
 alone; opt out with /etc/debion/keep-ifupdown).
